The bare script stopped at medium because all three vendors failed there, so it never evaluated the permitted higher rung. That is a ladder-design bug, not evidence about the target. I’m replacing the two intermediate presets with genuinely smaller uniform-layer cases whose exact counts are simple falling factorials; the hard target and its construction stay unchanged. Then I’ll rerun the authoritative bare loop.
